Translation patch: `Row::as_ref`, `Row::get`, `Row::get_opt`, `Row::take`, `Row::take_opt`

Change: The `Option` combinator chains (`and_then` with closures, `map(|x| from_value::<T>(x.clone()))`, `map(from_value::<T>)`, and the `from_value_opt` variants) become nested `match`es on the same `Option`s, calling the same functions in the same order.
Why: Aeneas does not model `Option::and_then`, nor closures / fn items passed as values (see patches 22, 53).
Behaviour: Identical. Each `match` returns `None` exactly where the chain short-circuits (`idx` gives `None`; `get`/`get_mut` gives `None`; the cell is `None`), and otherwise applies the same conversion to the same value (`x.clone()` for `get`/`get_opt`; for `take`/`take_opt`, the value moved out by `Option::take`, which leaves `None` in the cell exactly as before).

